{"id":17645,"name":"Catawba County","slug":"catawba-county","state":"North Carolina","code":"NC","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/north-carolina-tax-deed-sales/catawba-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-20T14:51:07","facts":{"taxSaleType":"Tax Foreclosure Sale","bidProcedure":"Premium Bid","deposit":"20%","extra":[{"label":"Typical Date of Sale","value":"No specific date"},{"label":"Sale Contact","value":"Catawba County Tax Department"},{"label":"Auction Site","value":"Catawba County Courthouse"},{"label":"County Website","value":"Catawba County"}]},"bodyHtml":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed aligncenter is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"ZyUawCcfkkK1Sv6XIUEV71Wd0BCmqnsR6xM4i7BhVvOZ3rfuHdhaF4WlXwpmLGzF9\"><iframe title=\"Real Estate Grabs! 40-90% Off at Auction - Catawba County - North Carolina Tax Deed Investing\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/ZcOfT4UuLWw?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Real Estate Grabs! 40-90% Off at Auction &#8211; Catawba County &#8211; North Carolina Tax Deed Investing</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Unlock property deals in Catawba County, NC, where tax foreclosure sales offer hidden gems at unbeatable prices. Dive in, no sign-up needed, and navigate the thrill of a 10-day bidding challenge to claim your prize!</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Catawba County, North Carolina’s ‘Tax Foreclosure Sales’ is your chance to buy properties below market value. The county is known for its collaborative economic efforts, making it a prime spot for investors. Sales are conducted at the Catawba County Justice Center in Newton, NC. There is no need for registration – the highest bidder wins!</p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you win, you must be prepared with a 20% deposit and cover the balance, recording fees, and revenue stamps before the sale&#8217;s confirmation. The auction isn&#8217;t the end; there&#8217;s a 10-day window for upset bids, where the next bid must top the current by 5% or at least $750. Upset bids must be made in person at the County Clerk of Superior Court. Visit the county website or contact the Catawba County Tax Department for more details and be ready to make your move.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Important-Details\">Important Details</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina-768x512.webp 768w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina-20x13.webp 20w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina-32x21.webp 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina.png 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina-541x360.png 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina-296x197.png 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina-768x512.png 768w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina-20x13.png 20w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Catawba-River-Train-Bridge-Catawba-North-Carolina-32x21.png 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-17655 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Catawba River Train Bridge, Catawba, North Carolina\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Book a Call with Dustin Hahn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Key-Information\">Key Information</h3>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Location</strong>: All sales are conducted on the front steps of the Catawba County Justice Center at 100 Government Drive, Newton, North Carolina, starting at 12:00 p.m. unless otherwise noted.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Deposit</strong>: They Require a 20% cash deposit immediately after the sale.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Balance</strong>: You must pay the balance, along with recording fees and revenue stamps, before the sale is confirmed.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Redemption</strong>: The property owner can redeem the property by paying taxes, interest fees, and foreclosure costs before the sale date.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Upset Bids</strong>: Bidders can place upset bids within ten days. You must place the upset bid in person at the County Clerk of Superior Court, and it must exceed the current bid by 5% or $750, whichever is higher.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<p>For more accurate and up-to-date details, check the official Catawba County resources or call the <a href=\"https://www.catawbacountync.gov/county-services/tax/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Tax Department</mark></a> directly​.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Frequently-Asked-Questions\">Frequently Asked Questions</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: What happens if I am the highest bidder?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: If you win, you must pay a 20% deposit immediately and settle the remaining balance plus fees before confirming the sale.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: Can the property owner stop the foreclosure?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: Yes, the property owner can redeem the property by paying all due taxes, interest, and fees before the sale date.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: What is an upset bid?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>A: An upset bid occurs when someone places a higher bid within ten days after the auction. It must be at least 5% higher than the current bid or $750 more.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Useful-Links\">Useful Links</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul clas